       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. At that dose the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and, in overdose, prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nCould you tell me which of these you intended?\n\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the usual maximum.\n- **A different dose.** For example, 2.5 mg or 5 mg may have been meant as a starting dose, and 30 mg may be a typo.\n- **A different drug.** Another agent may have been intended.\n- **30 mg on purpose.** If there's a specific clinical reason, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's an intentional above-maximum dose. I'd also suggest confirming it with pharmacy.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter it right away."
      }
